{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Managing the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Hiring New People", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional with if-clauses to exchange opinions about possible outcomes in the present or in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen. The condition is in the present. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future.<br/><br> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you focus more on our customers, they'll leave a larger tip.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The result (leaving a larger tip) depends on whether the condition is met (focus more on customers).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple, \u2026 will + base verb \u2026</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Will + base verb \u2026 If + Present Simple</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you are able to take a longer view of the hiring process, you will find talented and experienced employees.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you hire someone with restaurant experience, they will be familiar with the processes and skills needed for the job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you hire someone recommended by a current staff member, you will also get a lot of help with training.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you can ask interview questions that allow the candidate to show you their skills, you will have a clear idea of the contribution that person will be able to make.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Duty or Obligation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use a variety of modals to talk about duties and obligations, to express what someone is responsible for and to give strong advice and recommendations. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Let's look at the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should<span class=\"italic\">. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">must</span> when you decide for yourself what is necessary.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">must</span> show them I can live up to their expectations. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span> before verbs that talk about necessity. </span><span class=\"italic\">Have got to</span> is more casual.<span class=\"italic\"> Have to</span> implies that someone else imposed the necessity on you.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to buckle down</span> Kristi, and get it done. </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ve got to work</span> systematically.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is a modal you can use to give advice and to talk about duty.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> make sure you meet these deadlines. </span>(advice)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> take this responsibility seriously. </span> (duty)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You have to consider that applicant seriously.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You must seek out new employees that will fit into the culture and dynamic of your restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You have got to list which skills you require your employees to have.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "take the long view", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think about the effect that something will have in the future rather than what happens now", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you are able to take a longer view of the hiring process, you will find talented and experienced employees.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about who to hire. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hiring practice ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a particular way of finding people to employ ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have got to establish some effective hiring practices before you begin your recruitment search.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to result in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something happen ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should also evaluate if any nearby colleges or online job search websites have resulted in the hiring of quality employees.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to track", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to record the progress of something over time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must track the performance of all your recruitment sources.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "capacity ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a job or position", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you receive an application from someone who has worked in several capacities  you have to consider that applicant seriously.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fit into ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be a part of ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must seek out new employees that will fit into the culture and dynamic of your restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you have created your own company. Give your company a name.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide on 8-10 well-known people from the world of sports, politics, entertainment, science, history, business, and so on that you have to hire to help you in your company. You can assign them job titles if you want to be more creative (managers, regular employees, account manager, etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your \u201cstaff\u201d list in a group. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your choices. Say who you chose and why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In groups, choose 10 people to hire from everyone's staff list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember to include everyone in the discussion and try to reach a compromise about who to \u201cfire\u201d and who to keep.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I identify individuals and job titles for my new company.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my list of \u201cemployees\u201d in groups.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my choices.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I work with my classmates to decide which 10 employees we should keep.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Do you think it is important to hire someone with a lot of experience?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What are other things that should be considered when hiring a new employee? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " I can talk about work and dealing with customers.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled using when or if.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express duty or obligation in the present.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Who should they hire?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"c